1
00:03:31,304 --> 00:03:37,304
The Circle of Life Continues...

2
00:07:02,608 --> 00:07:08,608
The Lion King II: Simba's Pride is a family, adventure,
animation film directed by Darrell Rooney.

3
00:10:33,913 --> 00:10:39,913
The circle of life continues for Simba, now fully grown and in
his rightful place as the king of Pride Rock.

4
00:14:05,217 --> 00:14:11,217
Simba and Nala have given birth to a daughter, Kiara
who's as rebellious as her father was.

5
00:17:36,521 --> 00:17:42,521
But Kiara drives her parents to distraction when she catches the
eye of Kovu, the son of the evil lioness, Zira.

6
00:21:07,826 --> 00:21:13,826
Will Kovu steal Kiara's heart?

7
00:24:39,130 --> 00:24:45,130
Simba (voice), played by Matthew Broderick.

8
00:28:10,434 --> 00:28:16,434
Kiara (voice), played by Neve Campbell.

9
00:31:41,739 --> 00:31:47,739
Kovu (voice), played by Jason Marsden.

10
00:35:13,043 --> 00:35:19,043
Timon (voice), played by Nathan Lane.

11
00:38:44,347 --> 00:38:50,347
Pumbaa (voice), played by Ernie Sabella.

12
00:42:15,652 --> 00:42:21,652
Nuka (voice), played by Andy Dick.

13
00:45:46,956 --> 00:45:52,956
The Lion King II: Simba's Pride, also titled as The Lion King 2: Simba's Pride, is a 1998 American
animated direct-to-video musical drama film produced by Walt Disney Video Premiere.

14
00:49:18,260 --> 00:49:24,260
Directed by Darrell Rooney, it is the sequel to Disney Animation's 1994 film, The Lion King, with its plot
influenced by William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet, and the second installment in The Lion King trilogy.

15
00:52:49,565 --> 00:52:55,565
Animated by Walt Disney Animation Australia, the film centers on Simba and Nala's daughter
Kiara, who falls in love with Kovu, a lion from an exiled pride once loyal to Scar.

16
00:56:20,869 --> 00:56:26,869
Separated by Simba's prejudice against the pride and a vindictive plot planned by Kovu's mother
Zira, Kiara and Kovu struggle to unite their estranged prides and be together.

17
00:59:52,173 --> 00:59:58,173
Most of the original cast returned to their roles from
the first film with a few exceptions.

18
01:03:23,478 --> 01:03:29,478
Rowan Atkinson, who voiced Zazu in the first film, was replaced by Edward
Hibbert for both this film and The Lion King 1½ (2004).

19
01:06:54,782 --> 01:07:00,782
Jeremy Irons, who voiced Scar in the first film, was replaced by Jim
Cummings, who briefly provided his singing voice in the first film.

20
01:10:26,086 --> 01:10:32,086
While not drawing the same attention as its predecessor, Simba's Pride
received generally positive reviews from critics and audiences.

21
01:13:57,391 --> 01:14:03,391
The film explores themes of friendship, baby, africa, lion, cartoon.

22
01:17:28,695 --> 01:17:34,695
The tone is emotional.
